s layer and no position-heal effect. Damage is at least1 and P has no other able reserve."}, "ordinary_controls": [{"id": "M03-001-C1", "input": "Only one fainted player seat needs replacement; no prior switch in the pass; successful escape.", "expected": "No later fainted-player prompt exists; empty switched set ends replacement loop and decision remains3."}, {"id": "M03-001-C2", "input": "Same multi-faint state, but first prompt chooses Yes and a legal reserve.", "expected": "Ordinary replacement occurs without first setting escape decision3."}, {"id": "M03-001-C3", "input": "Positive result already present before ordinary replacement entry.", "expected": "Entry result guard returns immediately; this does not refute a result written inside the running scan."}], "minimal_counterexample": {"id": "M03-001-V1", "steps": "First prompt declines; calculation writes escape3 and returns1. The current seat does not replace, but the scan advances to seat2, asks again, accepts P and binds/sends P at seat2. The pass then runs entry-position and hazard processing.", "expected_observation": "Second prompt and the later replacement happen after the escape success feedback; no immediate return occurs at that first success. With nonlethal/no hazards and no other result producer, the enclosing EOR later returns with decision3.", "minimum_impact": "Extra input, member binding/display order and entry-effect submissions after successful escape feedback."}, "stronger_counterexample": {"id": "M03-001-V2", "steps": "Keep the same legal post-faint state and interaction, but use the HP1/Spikes variant. The later entry applies hazard damage, formally faints P, then calls the ordinary judge.", "expected_observation": "All player participants now unable while foe alive; ordinary judge overwrites3 with2. EOR sees2 only after replacement returns. HP0 and formal faint prefix are already committed.", "qualification": "This stronger vector is independently derived by proposer from fully read source; M01 challenge independently supports the nonlethal continuation, not the final lethal extension. No game/model/host execution."}, "lifecycle_trace": [{"role": "producer", "source": {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/005_Battle_ActionSwitching.rb", "lines": [187, 199], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, "behavior": "Per-seat decline calls the replacement escape path; positive return makes only that seat skip replacement."}, {"role": "write/display", "source": {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/007_Battle_ActionRunning.rb", "lines": [134, 155], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, "behavior": "Speed advantage writes3 after success feedback; duringBattle keeps the attempt count unchanged."}, {"role": "consumer/continuation", "source": {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/005_Battle_ActionSwitching.rb", "lines": [151, 204], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, "behavior": "The running scan lacks a result guard before later seats or before pass entry notification."}, {"role": "write/persistence", "source": {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/005_Battle_ActionSwitching.rb", "lines": [274, 296], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, "behavior": "Later legal replacement binds persistent member identity and changes temporary display order before entry callbacks."}, {"role": "consumer/persistence", "source": {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/005_Battle_ActionSwitching.rb", "lines": [337, 344], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, "behavior": "Position heal and hazards still run; hazard fainting can invoke ordinary judging."}, {"role": "later result writer", "source": {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/002_Battle_StartAndEnd.rb", "lines": [557, 567], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, "behavior": "Ordinary judge has no positive-result exemption and can overwrite3."}, {"role": "actual exit consumer", "source": {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/011_Battle_EndOfRoundPhase.rb", "lines": [704, 706], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, "behavior": "Outer EOR checks result only after replacement call returns."}], "failure_cancellation_partial_commit": "Cancelling the earlier decline is not a rollback operation: No initiates escape. A later required reserve chooser has its own cancellation permission. The escape feedback/result, later replacement and entry effects commit at their individual points; an exception later in display, selection or entry is governed by existing diagnostics and gives no transaction rollback guarantee. Do not claim final3 for every variant.", "negative_evidence": {"scope": "Entire ordinary Battle and Battler subtrees read; ordinary replacement loop and immediate callers/consumers inspected continuously. Only BattleArena overrides replacement in the locator search, and it is excluded.", "search_receipts": ["logs/047-dependency-search.json", "logs/055-consumers.json"], "counterevidence_preserved": "WP42 L51/L135 already provides the correct generic non-immediate-exit rule; this finding is only the concrete WP41 replacement-path contract."}, "impact": "An independent implementation that short-circuits all replacement work at first escape success would suppress later prompts and entry submissions and cannot reproduce the bounded reference outcome. This is a specification fidelity issue, not an instruction to repair reference code or permanently preserve its anomaly.", "minimal_correction": "Qualify WP41 L123: positive replacement escape sets a result, but the current multi-seat replacement scan can continue before the caller checks it. Give the two-seat continuation vector and state that later entry/judge effects may change the result. Preserve all normal escape probability and guard rules.", "recommended_read_set": [{"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/005_Battle_ActionSwitching.rb", "lines": [142, 217], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/007_Battle_ActionRunning.rb", "lines": [60, 158], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/005_Battle_ActionSwitching.rb", "lines": [219, 467], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/002_Battle_StartAndEnd.rb", "lines": [557, 567], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, {"path": "Data/Scripts/011_Battle/001_Battle/011_Battle_EndOfRoundPhase.rb", "lines": [700, 706], "commit": "8c5911e4a4b07b07e832e4bb0d5d8859e88b4a9b"}, {"path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp41-switching-positioning-and-escape.md", "lines": [114, 132], "commit": "e646432c644dec04d306842cc5a559a29c718fbc"}, {"path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp42-growth-end-of-round-and-battle-outcomes.md", "lines": [45, 55], "commit": "e646432c644dec04d306842cc5a559a29c718fbc"}, {"path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp42-growth-end-of-round-and-battle-outcomes.md", "lines": [125, 135], "commit": "e646432c644dec04d306842cc5a559a29c718fbc"}], "recommended_write_set": [{"path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp41-switching-positioning-and-escape.md", "scope": "Only §5.1 success wording and necessary nearby invariant cross-reference."}, {"path": "deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/combat-requirements-wp39-40-41-42-45.md", "scope": "Add one bounded multi-faint escape continuation vector plus independent nonlethal/lethal/control variants; update the SW count/list only if a new ID is added."}], "acceptance": ["No wording implies an immediate inner-loop exit at first successful replacement escape.", "Single-faint and entry-positive-result controls retain their current outcomes.", "Multiple-faint vector observes second prompt/binding after success; lethal variant distinguishes